<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/kawhi-leonard/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/kawhi-leonard/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Kawhi Leonard’s Salary at the Raptors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Leonard earns $50.3m in 2026-27, the largest salary on the Raptors payroll after the Clippers traded him to Toronto in September. It is the last year of the extension he signed with the Clippers, and up from $50m last season. His career earnings reach $428.6m across sixteen seasons. The salary is 25.00% of the club’s $201.19m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Kawhi Leonard Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"His Clippers contract ends this season, and his two-year Toronto extension takes over in 2027-28 at about $56.1m, rising to about $58.9m in 2028-29. That second year is a player option, so he could become a free agent in 2028 at 37."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Kawhi Leonard Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $50.3m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Kawhi Leonard’s Contract Worth at the Raptors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Leonard signed a two-year extension with Toronto worth $115m on September 22, 2026, a week after the trade. It covers 2027-28 and 2028-29, with a player option in the second year, and is about $11.1m below the maximum he could have signed for. This season he is paid under the three-year maximum extension worth $149.51m that he signed with the Clippers in January 2024, and he waived its 15% trade bonus so the trade could go through. He can become an unrestricted free agent in 2028 at 37 if he declines the option, or in 2029 at 38."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Kawhi Leonard’s Net Worth in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Published estimates put Leonard’s net worth at around $160m, against $428.6m in career earnings. His endorsement income has been substantial for most of the last decade. Indiana drafted him 15th in 2011 out of San Diego State and traded him to San Antonio on draft night. He was 20, and the first contract he signed paid $8.32m across four years."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is Kawhi Leonard on a Maximum Deal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Leonard is paid $50.3m because he has won two championships and two Finals Most Valuable Player awards with two different clubs, and the maximum is what that record buys even at 35. He is one of a small number of players to have won the Finals award with two different clubs."}}]}</script>
